  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-17999\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"17999\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"3275\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-17999\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-1\">Introduction</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"17999\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p>Let's recap some of the rules for exponents.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Product rule</strong>: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Quotient rule</strong>: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Power rule</strong>: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Power of product rule</strong>: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Power of quotient rule</strong>: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this.</p>\n\n        </div>",
